activation	Print prompt	2026-10-27T11:36:29.8105315Z {"title": "[Python / Windows]: Access Violation (0xC0000005) on kernel interrupt during spatial extension query execution", "body": "### What happens?\n\n#### **Description**\n\n**Environment:**\n- **OS**: Windows 11 / Windows Server (x86_64)\n- **DuckDB Version**: 1.5.5\n- **Python Version**: 3.13.9\n- **Environment**: Jupyter / ipykernel 7.3.0 (VS Code / JupyterLab)\n- **Extension**: `spatial` (v1.5.5)\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**\nWhen executing a long-running spatial query (e.g., spatial join with `ST_Intersects` on hundreds of thousands of geometry rows) within a Jupyter/ipykernel session on Windows, interrupting the execution (via `Kernel -> Interrupt` or `SIGINT` / `GenerateConsoleCtrlEvent`) causes the Python process to crash with `ExitCode: 3221225477` (`STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION` / `0xC0000005`).\n\nAdditionally, calling `INSTALL spatial;` in a notebook environment attempts to display interactive widget progress bars (`FloatProgress`), which fails when CDN access (`unpkg.com`) is blocked or restricted in corporate environments.\n\n\n**Expected Behavior:**\nThe query should cleanly abort and raise a `KeyboardInterrupt` / query cancellation error without terminating or crashing the host Python process.\n\n---\n\n**Actual Behavior:**\nThe host Python kernel terminates abruptly with `ExitCode: 3221225477` (`0xC0000005`):\n\n```text\n[info] Interrupt kernel execution\n[info] Interrupting kernel via custom event (Win32)\n[error] Disposing session as kernel process died ExitCode: 3221225477\n```\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n\n---\n\n**Minimal Reproducible Example (MRE):**\n\n```python\nimport duckdb\n\ncon = duckdb.connect()\n\n# 1. Install & Load spatial extension\ncon.sql(\"INSTALL spatial;\")\ncon.sql(\"LOAD spatial;\")\n\n# 2. Create synthetic dataset (points and bounding polygons)\ncon.sql(\"\"\"\n    CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE test_points AS\n    SELECT \n        range AS id,\n        ST_Point(2.0 + (range % 1000) * 0.001, 48.0 + (range % 1000) * 0.001) AS geom\n    FROM range(250000);\n\"\"\")\n\ncon.sql(\"\"\"\n    CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE test_polygons AS\n    SELECT \n        range AS poly_id,\n        ST_Buffer(ST_Point(2.0 + (range % 100) * 0.01, 48.0 + (range % 100) * 0.01), 0.05) AS poly_geom\n    FROM range(1000);\n\"\"\")\n\n# 3. Heavy spatial join\nquery = \"\"\"\n    SELECT p.id, poly.poly_id\n    FROM test_points p\n    LEFT JOIN test_polygons poly\n    ON ST_Intersects(p.geom, poly.poly_geom);\n\"\"\"\n\n# While this query is executing, send an Interrupt (Kernel -> Interrupt / Ctrl+C):\ncon.sql(query).show()\n```\n\n---\n\n### OS:\n\nWindows\n\n### DuckDB Version:\n\n1.5.5\n\n### DuckDB Client:\n\nPython\n\n### Hardware:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Full Name:\n\nMathis Derenne\n\n### Affiliation:\n\nCoSpirit\n\n### Did you include all relevant configuration (e.g., CPU architecture, Linux distribution) to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all code required to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all relevant data sets for reproducing the issue?\n\nYes"}
